      "side": 1,
      "message": "Chromium canary actually looks ok (one compile failure, but the blink bots were happy). The other canaries look like infra issues or existing compile failure on G3, but chromium is the only one I was really worried about.",
      "revId": "d78082530d04da45bfd62c973cfcc0c45d258b5a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e565beba_ca5e8653",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-02T19:09:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FYI: This does change the GPU many_stops GMs, but I honestly think the new ones look a little better. (Still not as nice as CPU, given the filtering, but not as blurry). The linked gold results are misleading, because the new closest image is the CPU. When I diff\u0027d against the existing GPU results, the old images had very uneven spacing of stops.",
      "revId": "d78082530d04da45bfd62c973cfcc0c45d258b5a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4f52202d_1d61d07c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-02T19:18:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I\u0027m following this and the way I remember the GPU shader\u0027s being evaluated, this means that the texture fallback stores the results of interpolating the color stops in the intermediate color space. Once it\u0027s read from the texture, we just flow through the existing sksl to handle converting from the intermediate to the dst?\n\nAnd we\u0027ve already transformed the colors/positions to account for the interpolation directions, so they shouldn\u0027t impact the cache key. And we don\u0027t really need to include the interpolation mode in the key anyways, since even if two different interpolations arrived at exactly the same set of intermediate color values/positions, that means this bitmap lookup is correct for both. The extra color space conversion is handled by the rest of the shader that still knows about the interpolation to differentiate the two.",
      "revId": "d78082530d04da45bfd62c973cfcc0c45d258b5a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7401fbfc_dae03b46",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-02T19:25:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that they seem to be lining up better with the CPU\u0027s placement and that a little more blurriness is not unexpected given the texture fallback.\n\nThe sampling for hardstop_gradients_many is a little odd, though. Are we just getting unlucky with the mapping from the full-width gradient to the reduced dimensionality of the cache? Or do we need to offset by 1/2px maybe?",
      "parentUuid": "e565beba_ca5e8653",
      "revId": "d78082530d04da45bfd62c973cfcc0c45d258b5a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "34814e20_c1f0acf2",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-02T19:35:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suspect that\u0027s what\u0027s happening. I could try playing with the mapping - I wondered if we should be mapping the first texture entry to 0, rather then 0.5, but this feels more correct, given that we\u0027re going to directly map the local coordinates to texture coordinates when we use this colorizer (and the fact that RP is evaluating at pixel centers).",
      "parentUuid": "7401fbfc_dae03b46",
      "revId": "d78082530d04da45bfd62c973cfcc0c45d258b5a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92b8bbab_ff086b4b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-02T19:35:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, that\u0027s the situation right now, but you\u0027ll notice that the gradients_color_space_many_stops GM is wrong on GPU (in 8888 configs). That\u0027s because the interpolated values can be stored in a fixed-point format like that. The follow-up will be to plumb the interpolation struct here (and put it in the key), and move that portion of the RP code into the new helper as well. Then the texture fallback path will produce a texture in destination space, and we\u0027ll skip the final transformation if we used a texture colorizer.",
      "parentUuid": "4f52202d_1d61d07c",
      "revId": "d78082530d04da45bfd62c973cfcc0c45d258b5a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3404bf4a_b8c601f1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-02T19:39:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed, with seed_shader setting up the pixel-center values, I feel like it\u0027s consistent and just a resolution issue. Locally, if you bump up the size of the texture to a much larger dimension, does it get closer to the CPU result? If so, that would be evidence that that\u0027s the issue, vs. some bug in the use of the RP and its stop searching.",
      "parentUuid": "34814e20_c1f0acf2",
      "revId": "d78082530d04da45bfd62c973cfcc0c45d258b5a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "20f44751_50871a69",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-02T19:43:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yup. Bumped to 1k, and it\u0027s now *very* close (with a handful of much smaller deltas on specific transitions).",
      "parentUuid": "3404bf4a_b8c601f1",
      "revId": "d78082530d04da45bfd62c973cfcc0c45d258b5a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "829499f1_b18fde1b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-02T19:55:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We\u0027ve had plenty of complaints about the quality of the texture fallback case. Do you think it\u0027s reasonable to move up to 1024 or 512? Or have a heuristic based on the number of stops/projected size? Maybe that would be going farther than useful for Ganesh these days. A size increase is easy but could have negative impacts on memory usage.",
      "parentUuid": "20f44751_50871a69",
      "revId": "d78082530d04da45bfd62c973cfcc0c45d258b5a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7939e7d_b30b6747",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-03T13:12:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could play with it, although I think I agree - I\u0027m not real interested in spending time tuning this (and then fighting with memory complaints).\n\nOne other point though: This CL has also fixed a long-standing bug in the linear_gradient and linear_gradient_nodither GMs on low-end GPUs (that need to use the texture fallback at smaller stop counts). They used to have a really jagged effect down the left edge (as the stop count increases), which is no longer there. I\u0027m not surprised -- as I was looking at the old code, I noticed several strange issues with how the texture was populated: consecutive \"filling\" loops would always overlap a point, so in the limit, every pixel would be written twice, and no pixel would ever have a blended color (just a pure-stop color). I\u0027m sure the sampling got strange.\n\nhttps://gold.skia.org/search?blame\u003d001000011384\u0026corpus\u003dgm",
      "parentUuid": "829499f1_b18fde1b",
      "revId": "d78082530d04da45bfd62c973cfcc0c45d258b5a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
